  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Contains 40 epiphanies on 40 numbered pages (printed on unbound bifolia) and 4 sections of artwork (etching, lithography, collage in various formats) respectively titled Death, Dreams, Games, and Planes.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Printing by Daniel Keleher &amp; Bruce Chandler, Wild Carrot Letterpress. Type by Dan Carr &amp; Julia Ferrarie, Golgonooza Letter Foundry. Calligraphy by Jerry Kelly. Etching by Marjorie Van Dyke assisted by Maria Luisa Rojo, The Printmaking Workshop. Lithography by Rhae Burden. Collage by Zahra Partovi. Paper is Moulin du Gue and Japanese papers. Binding by David Bourbeau, Thistle Bindery.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The epiphanies are copyright 1956.</subfield>
  </datafield>
